traceability.evidence:
Story file docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md exists and its content (acceptance criteria plus REQs REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING, REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE, REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE, REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE) matches the specification provided in the assessment prompt (re-read in this run).,Dedicated test suite tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts exists and is explicitly tied to this story: - Header includes: * "Tests for: docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md" * "@story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md" * "@req REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING ..." * "@req REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT ..." * "@supports docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT". - Top-level describe: "Auto-fix behavior (Story 008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX)".,Key excerpts from tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts confirm behavior for each requirement: - REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING (missing @story auto-insertion via require-story-annotation): * Valid cases ensure already-annotated functions/methods are unchanged: - name: "[REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] already annotated function is unchanged" - name: "[REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING] already annotated class method is unchanged" * Invalid cases assert auto-fix inserts a JSDoc @story immediately above various node types and that the suggested fix output matches: - FunctionDeclaration: output `/** @story docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md */
function autoFixMe() {}` - FunctionExpression assigned to const: output `/** @story docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md */
const fnExpr = function() {};` - Class MethodDefinition: output `class C {
 /** @story docs/stories/003.0-DEV-FUNCTION-ANNOTATIONS.story.md */
 method() {}
}` - TSDeclareFunction and TSMethodSignature with TypeScript parser configured, with corresponding outputs inserting the same @story block immediately before the declaration/interface.,Additional tests in tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts cover configuration-related requirements: - REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE: * Test name: "[REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE] uses configured templates for functions and methods" within the require-story-annotation invalid cases verifies that when rule options annotationTemplate and methodAnnotationTemplate are set, the fixer uses those templates rather than the built-in placeholder. - REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE for require-story-annotation: * Test name: "[REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE] does not insert annotations when autoFix is false" asserts that with rule option autoFix: false, missing-annotation diagnostics are reported but the output does not include inserted @story comments.,The same test file covers REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT and selective behavior for valid-annotation-format: - Block "[REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT] valid-annotation-format auto-fix": * Valid: - "[REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT] already-correct story path is unchanged" ensures no changes for correctly suffixed @story values. * Invalid: - "[REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT] adds .md extension for .story path" verifies `.story` is normalized to `.story.md`. - "[REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT] adds .story.md extension when missing entirely" verifies bare paths gain `.story.md`. - "[REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE] does not apply suffix fix when autoFix is false" ensures that with autoFix: false, no suffix normalization occurs, even though the format is invalid.,User-facing documentation in user-docs/api-reference.md documents the auto-fix behavior, templates, and toggles as required: - traceability/require-story-annotation section: * Description explicitly ties behavior to Story 008.0: "When run with `--fix`, the rule inserts a single-line placeholder JSDoc `@story` annotation above missing functions, methods, TypeScript declare functions, and interface method signatures using a built-in template aligned with Story 008.0. This template is now configurable on a per-rule basis, and the rule exposes an explicit auto-fix toggle...". * Options include: - `annotationTemplate` (string) – overrides the default placeholder JSDoc template for functions/non-methods, referencing the built-in Story 008.0 template when omitted. - `methodAnnotationTemplate` (string) – overrides the template for methods/TS method signatures, falling back appropriately. - `autoFix` (boolean) – disables all automatic fix behavior when false, retains diagnostics and suggestions when true (or omitted). * This directly fulfills REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE, REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE, and documents REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING / REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE / REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE behavior. - traceability/valid-annotation-format section: * Description: "When run with `--fix`, the rule limits changes to safe `@story` path suffix normalization only—for example, adding `.md` when the path ends with `.story`, or adding `.story.md` when the base path has no extension—using targeted replacements implemented in the `getFixedStoryPath` and `reportInvalidStoryFormatWithFix` helpers. It does not change directories, infer new story names, or modify any surrounding comment text or whitespace, in line with Story 008.0. Selective disabling of this suffix-normalization auto-fix behavior is available via the `autoFix` option...". * Options: - Includes `autoFix` (boolean) that, when false, disables all suffix-normalization fixes but keeps validation, matching REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE. * This aligns with REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT, REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE, and REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE and clearly documents the constraints.,Implementation-level behavior for safety and preservation is validated by the combination of tests: - REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE and REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE for require-story-annotation: * Tests assert that already annotated code remains unchanged (`already annotated function/method is unchanged`). * Fixes only insert a new single-line JSDoc comment directly before the function/method, without altering the function body or other comments. - REQ-AUTOFIX-SAFE and REQ-AUTOFIX-PRESERVE for valid-annotation-format: * Only the @story path suffix is changed; tests explicitly show only `.story`→`.story.md` or bare→`.story.md` adjustments. * No tests, docs, or behavior indicate directory changes, new filenames, or modifications outside the string value, consistent with story constraints.,Full Jest test suite was re-run with verbose output using `npm test -- --verbose` and completed successfully (exit code 0). Summary: - Test Suites: 1 skipped, 48 passed, 48 of 49 total. - Tests: 2 skipped, 352 passed, 354 total. - Within this run, the dedicated story test suite passed: - PASS tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts * All REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING, REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT, REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE, and REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE tests succeeded, confirming the implemented behavior remains consistent and regression-free.,Additional integration and supporting tests confirm correct integration and non-regression with the wider plugin: - tests/rules/require-story-annotation.test.ts validates core rule behavior and ensures that adding auto-fix did not break validation or configuration aspects defined in dependency stories (003.0 and 007.0). - tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts extensively validates annotation parsing/validation and coexists with the auto-fix behavior, confirming that format validation plus suffix-only fixing is working as intended (dependency 005.0). - Integration tests (e.g., tests/integration/cli-integration.test.ts and tests/integration/dogfooding-validation.test.ts) show the plugin—including these rules—operating correctly through - ESLint CLI, - project presets, - and CI-style dogfooding, which implies the auto-fix-enabled rules integrate cleanly with the rest of the ESLint toolchain and project configuration.,Traceability between this story and tests is explicit: - tests/rules/auto-fix-behavior-008.test.ts has `@story docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md` and `@supports docs/stories/008.0-DEV-AUTO-FIX.story.md REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT` in its header, and the top-level describe includes the story number. Test names reference REQ-AUTOFIX-MISSING, REQ-AUTOFIX-FORMAT, REQ-AUTOFIX-TEMPLATE, and REQ-AUTOFIX-SELECTIVE, providing clear mapping from requirements to executing tests.
